# Layer A is prose and one workflow, and it is copied verbatim into two repositories that
# format Markdown differently — one runs Prettier over `*.md`, the other does not. Shared
# prose under two formatters reflows on every commit and breaks the vendored copy's sha
# check on every sync, so the plugin owns its own formatting and the consumers exclude it.
#
# `proseWrap: preserve` is the half of that decision that matters. Prettier's default
# reflows every paragraph to `printWidth`, which would rewrite every file here on the
# first run and make every future diff a paragraph rather than a sentence. Preserving the
# hand wrapping keeps a one-word edit a one-line diff, which is what makes a review of
# doctrine readable at all.

# The stacks are mounted for reading. They own their own formatting.
python-harness/
frontend-harness/

